{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "bd59f2d6-3c44-8fcd-bc0e-54595f3530d8",
  "created_at": "2026-01-16T15:08:13-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Zoning and Inspections",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Celeste Semedo",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Anita Chaudhry",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-16T15:05:25-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Zoning and Inspections, this is Anita. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-16T15:05:29-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hi, yes, hello. Sorry, I'm on speakerphone and I'm walking, so if it thumps, that's just my feet. [pause] Okay, can you hear me?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-16T15:05:37-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I can hear you, a little thumpy but fine. Go ahead."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-16T15:05:41-05:00",
      "duration": 16,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Great. So I own a house on Bacheller Street, number 295, over in the Fifth Ward, and I rent it out. I want to put up a fence along the back property line. A six-foot one. Or, whatever is allowed that's tall, honestly. I'm thinking composite, not wood."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-16T15:05:57-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. And is this a fence you're putting up yourself, or a contractor?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-16T15:06:02-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Oh, um, a contractor, I think. Or maybe me and my cousin. I haven't decided. Does that matter? [laughs] Wait, what was my actual question. Right. Does a fence need a permit, or do I just call the city and tell you I'm doing it?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-16T15:06:17-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Good question. Generally a fence does need a permit here, so it's not just a heads-up call. Height is part of it, and where it sits relative to the property line. Is the whole back line what you're fencing, or does it turn along the sides?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-16T15:06:32-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Just the back. Straight across. I think. [crosstalk] Sorry, go ahead."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-16T15:06:36-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I was going to say, do you have a survey or plot plan of the lot? We'll want to see where the line is and where the fence goes."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-16T15:06:46-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "A plot plan, hmm. I might have something from when I bought it. Is that the same as a survey? I always mix those up."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-16T15:06:55-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Close. A survey is the one a surveyor drew up, showing the boundaries. A plot plan can be a simpler sketch of the lot. If you have the closing papers, there's often one in there. Bring whatever you find and we can tell you if it works."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-16T15:07:10-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, okay. Closing papers. Got it. And, um, how long does approval take? Like, if I applied next week, am I waiting days, or weeks?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-16T15:07:19-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "For a straightforward fence, usually a matter of days to a couple of weeks once the application is complete. Missing paperwork is what slows it down, so that's why I mention the plan."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-16T15:07:30-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Days to a couple weeks. Okay. Oh, and does the six feet thing, is that definitely allowed, or is that the part where you say it depends?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-16T15:07:39-05:00",
      "duration": 17,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It does depend a bit, on whether it's the back or the front and the zoning of the lot. The back is usually where taller is allowed, but the reviewer will confirm when you apply. Do you want me to note your number for a callback if you have more questions?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-16T15:07:56-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sure, that'd be great. It's 401-555-0153."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-16T15:07:59-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Got it, 401-555-0153. And you're at 295 Bacheller. I'll leave a note with that."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-16T15:08:04-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Perfect. Thank you so much. Sorry about the thumping, I'm almost at my car. [laughs] Bye!"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-16T15:08:10-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No problem at all. Have a good weekend."
    }
  ],
